course: dictionary
lesson: 12425
title: Deadpan
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Deadpan means saying something funny with a completely serious face and a flat voice, as if nothing is funny at all. «"I have just won the lottery," said Sam, deadpan, and went back to his cereal.» Sam does not look excited. Because he looks so calm, the reader knows he is joking.
explain: Deadpan can describe a face, a voice, or the way someone speaks. A deadpan look shows no feeling at all. «Mum gave a deadpan stare when I told her the dog had eaten my homework.» It can also be a verb: «Grandma deadpanned, "Lovely weather for ducks," as the rain poured down.»
explain: The joke works because of the gap between the words and the face. Something silly or huge, said as if it were ordinary, is funnier. When a character says something silly with a straight face, ask yourself: are they joking?
fact: Deadpan means serious and blank, with no expression on the face.
fact: «Deadpan» can be an adjective (a deadpan face), an adverb (said deadpan), a noun (deadpan humour) or a verb (to deadpan).
fact: A deadpan voice is flat, so it does not go up or down to show feeling.
fact: Deadpan humour is often used in British humour, where a joke is told with a straight face.
fact: A deadpan speaker looks serious, but the listener can tell they are joking.
exercise: «"The sky is green today," said Ruby, deadpan.» How was Ruby speaking? | Sadly, with tears | *With a serious, blank face and a flat voice | Loudly and excitedly | Whispering in fear
exercise: «Her deadpan face showed no feeling at all.» What does deadpan mean here? | Sleepy | Angry and red | Very happy | *Blank, with no expression
exercise: Find the verb in this sentence: «Dad deadpanned, "Great, more homework."» | Dad | Great | *deadpanned | homework
test: «"I won the race by a mile," Tom said, deadpan, though he had come last.» Why is this funny? | *The claim is huge but said with a serious face, so it is clearly a joke | It is a sad story | The race was short | Tom ran very fast
test: Which sentence uses deadpan as an adverb? | I love deadpan humour | Her deadpan look told me nothing | *He said, "Nice shoes," deadpan | The deadpan face stared at me
exam: What is the best meaning of deadpan? | Wet and grey | Very fast | Happy and loud | *Serious and blank, often used for a joke
